  "_readme": [
    "Macro RELEASE SCHEDULE for the Simmer catalyst gate. This file holds dates,",
    "never data — nothing here is a print, a consensus, or a surprise.",
    "",
    "WHY A HARDCODED TABLE (see docs/simmer.md, 'Macro calendar'): no free",
    "machine-readable source exists. The Fed publishes no ICS/JSON/feed, and",
    "bls.gov actively 403s scripted requests under an explicit anti-bot policy",
    "(api.bls.gov serves data, not the schedule). The dates essentially never",
    "move and forward visibility is enormous, so ~15 minutes of work each",
    "December refreshes the whole year.",
    "",
    "CONFIRMED vs DERIVED. Every row carries `confirmed`. A confirmed row was",
    "read off the issuing agency's own schedule page and carries `source`. A",
    "derived row carries `derived: true`, a `derivation` string naming the rule,",
    "and `uncertainty_days` — the half-width of the window the gate must block,",
    "because an unconfirmed release date is a DISTRIBUTION, not a date.",
    "",
    "As of the generated_at date: FOMC is confirmed through Dec 2027 (the Fed",
    "publishes years ahead). BLS (CPI/PPI/NFP) and BEA (PCE) had published only",
    "through Dec 2026 — every 2027 row in those four series is DERIVED. Replace",
    "them with the published dates once BLS/BEA post the 2027 schedules (BLS",
    "typically posts the following year in the autumn).",
    "",
    "`confirmed_through` is the last date on which every row is agency-verified.",
    "`valid_through` is the last date the table covers at all; the engine refuses",
    "to score any expiry beyond it (simmer_calendar.refuse_beyond_table).",
    "",
    "FOMC rows use the ANNOUNCEMENT day (day two) as `date`, with `start_date`",
    "for day one; `sep: true` marks Summary of Economic Projections / dot-plot",
    "meetings, which carry the wider tails."
  ],
